[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b10: validating the opposition proxy
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   with REAL discovery coordinates
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   Steps b5 and b8 reconstructed discovery footprints from
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   provisional-designation half-months, using opposition longitude
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   lam_opp as a proxy for the true discovery longitude lam_d.
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   The stated caveat was that off-opposition pointings could make
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   the true footprint wider than reconstructed.  The OSSOS
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   characterized ensemble (J/ApJS/236/18) contains REAL discovery
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   RA/Dec, discovery JD and heliocentric distance for 840 objects
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   -- enough to validate the proxy directly and close that caveat.
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   V1  Proxy validation: |lam_d - lam_opp| per OSSOS object.
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   If the error is small, the reconstructed footprints in
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   b5/b8 are essentially exact, not approximate.
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   V2  The TRUE coupling measured on real discovery longitudes:
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   Delta_true = varpi - lam_d, by a-bin and by r/q.  This is
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   the externally-measured version of the smear that pointing
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   bias can apply to varpi.
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   V3  Externally-calibrated ceiling: apply the OSSOS-measured
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   Delta_true distribution (near-perihelion subset) to each
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   detached SBDB object's own lam_opp (itself smeared by the
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   measured proxy error) -- the tightest data-driven bound on
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   what pointing alone can do to R(varpi).
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   V4  The OSSOS a>150 micro-sample with true discovery
[2026-09-21 14:31:05 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 015]   longitudes listed explicitly.
